{11 = 11-19}
1111.	In his anger the Date Palm answered him. 
1112.	He addressed his brother the Tamarisk: 
1113.	@q[Date Palm,Tamarisk]{“You say: 
1114.	@q[Tamarisk,Date Palm]{“If people build daises for me and beautify them too, 
1115.	they certainly do not swear by the gods before clay (?).”} 
1116.	-- You may be the body of the gods in their shrines and people may name with a good name the daises of the gods, 
1117.	but it is silver that can pride itself as the overlay of the gods. 
1118.	……, 
1119.	describe your beauty!”} 
